# Force LF everywhere, regardless of platform or local git config. Without
# this, Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true, GitHub's windows-latest
# default) get CRLF for text files, including templates/**/*.md — which are
# embedded verbatim via include_str!() and hashed into generated adapter
# content (see claude_code.rs's content_hash()). A CRLF checkout changes that
# hash, producing different (but equally valid) output on Windows than on
# Unix: harmless in production, but it broke a snapshot test comparing
# Windows output against a Unix-recorded snapshot — the real fix is making
# checkouts byte-identical everywhere, not normalizing around the symptom.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary / generated — never touch line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
Cargo.lock -diff
